From 263d603dd3d145b0a38d2cd9512ff45ee5692148 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:36:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(interaction): predict held trapdoor placement

Native Bedrock 1.26.60.5 keeps trapdoor facing and half during held placement, including camera rotation and switching trapdoor materials. Repeated placement adds closed neighbors rather than toggling the previous block; releasing the control restores ordinary interaction.

Send the physical use-control lifetime through the shared block-use channel and retire it on release, screens, disconnect, and connection replacement. Suppress local block activation after a successful trapdoor placement and reuse its orientation while preserving water, power, and material properties. Keep this state until the control ends rather than resetting on selected-item changes or server teleports.

Real block-state tests cover material changes, orientation retention, independent placement properties, release, and ordinary blocks. Native captures and a failing Java baseline establish the intended behavior; spatial continuation and correction comparisons remain acceptance gates.

Native spatial captures permit continued placement from separate trapdoors,
including differently oriented ones, while unrelated floor targets remain
inactive. Keep the original support eligible for retries and suppress
other non-trapdoor targets until release. Send the actual prediction result
immediately before its concluding Java packet so failed repeats do not
reset server placement state or predict item consumption.
